  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Born in Treviso and trained in economics at Ca’ Foscari University, De’Longhi joined the family manufacturing concern that began as a small workshop. He redirected it from components and heating products towards branded domestic appliances, combining engineering with an international distribution strategy. Acquisitions including Kenwood broadened the portfolio, while the group’s listing gave the business a public-market platform.\n\nCoffee equipment became the strongest global expression of that expansion, alongside cooking, climate-control and cleaning products sold across more than one hundred countries. De’Longhi also separated the professional heating and cooling operations into DelClima, whose majority stake was later sold to Mitsubishi Electric. He eventually handed operational leadership to the next generation; Fabio de’ Longhi became chairman and chief executive in April 2025.",
    "html": "<p>Born in Treviso and trained in economics at Ca’ Foscari University, De’Longhi joined the family manufacturing concern that began as a small workshop. He redirected it from components and heating products towards branded domestic appliances, combining engineering with an international distribution strategy. Acquisitions including Kenwood broadened the portfolio, while the group’s listing gave the business a public-market platform.</p>\r\n<p>Coffee equipment became the strongest global expression of that expansion, alongside cooking, climate-control and cleaning products sold across more than one hundred countries. De’Longhi also separated the professional heating and cooling operations into DelClima, whose majority stake was later sold to Mitsubishi Electric. He eventually handed operational leadership to the next generation; Fabio de’ Longhi became chairman and chief executive in April 2025.</p>\r\n",
